A||N||7||camon||Bought fiero need help.||||5||
Z||000000||camon||09-29-2001||12:34 AM||||Hello all!<P>I'm new to this board and just rescently bought a 1987 Fiero GT for a grand. All in all it is really in good condition with a few problems (which can be expected for only paying a thousand dollars)a paintjob is needed as the black paint has faded in a few spots. The interior is perfect and even has a hint of the new car smell yet...and no blemishes what so ever...the car appears to have been pampered it does have 109,000 miles on it though.<P>As I said there are a few problems that need attention!<P>Here are the things that I need to repair and any info would be great.<P>When I start the fiero in the morning while cold the engine starts right up but if I don't keep my foot on the gas pedal the engine will die. It starts right back up but it will continue doing this until I force it to stay running. This only lasts for less the a minute....after which I can release the throttle and it will hold it's own idle.<BR>Also if you drive it before it has warmed up completely a hesitation is noticed when applying the throttle. This problem also clears up when the car is warm. Any idea's????<P><BR>It also I think has a bad wheel bearing (not sure which one) I haven't had the time yet to jack it up and inspect (but it is a wheel bearing grind like noise). How difficult is the bearing to replace? I have a hayes manual and it seems pretty straight foward and easy. Has anyone done one of these and have any input on this subject?<P>It also has a key that was broken off in the driverside door lock. Anyway to get it out of there. The car has power locks so currently I an unlocking the passenger door and usintg the unlock switch......any ideas?<P>Well thank you all for your time and anything you can assist with.<P>Thanks!||||reg||5
Z||000001||BlackARROW||09-29-2001||01:21 AM||||My car will do the same thing when it will get below -20°C here.  But at normal temp - hmm..<P>Problem firing at low temp?  First, since it's a new car - if you don't know its condition, look for the usual basic:  spark plugs, wires, distributor, air filter, oil consistency. Than what?  For your "keep my foot on the gas pedal" - is the choke locking on? Maybe you need an adjustment there.<P>For your key that broke into the lock, if you see it, you could try getting it out with needles or 2 small thin knives.  A Professionnal Locksmith is an idea. Or if you are good at stunt, you could try like the Dukes, and drive on 2 wheels. Other than that, what else guys?<P>Lucky you got that deal for a gran  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I got a 4cyl for the same price :P   But a Canadian gran  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  hehe..<P>Good Luck, and welcome in the family<P><P>------------------<BR>BlackARROW &gt;&gt;--&gt;<BR>Gadgeteered Fiero 2M4 '85<BR>"Get your groove on"||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||09-29-2001||01:23 AM||||Your start-up/running cold problem and the hesitation could be caused by a dirty throttle body, old spark plugs, dirty injectors, old fuel filter. I would suggest give it a good tune-up and get a can of throttle body cleaner from Gumout. To clean the throttle body remove the rubber tube, place a towel under the TB (Engine NOT running) then hold open the throttle plate and spray. Then spray some more. Let stand about 10 minutes and start the car. It may start like it's flooded. (might have to give it lots of gas at first and clouds of smoke will emerge from the exhaust) A can of Gumout fuel system cleaner in the tank should help clean the injectors.<P>Front wheel bearings are easy and not expensive. rear bearings are expensive because you need to buy the entire hub assembly. If the sound is coming from the rear, you can also check the brake dust shields. Sometines they get bent or warp and scrape the rotor. Just bend them back out of the way.<P>As for the key, If you can't grab the key with a pair on needle nose pliers, you could try to metal pics or tweezers. If you still can't get it out, Just buy a lock set from AutoZone or NAPA. You'll need to replace both so they are keyed the same.<P>Good Luck and Welcome to the Forum!<P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">        <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||camon||09-29-2001||02:42 AM||||Thanks for the input.<P>Yeah when I seen it in our local paper for sale I though for sure that the thing was in really bad condition. Well to my surprise when I arrived at the guys house and seen it I then started thinking price mis-print. It was owned by an older guy (I say about late 50's)and he said he wanted to sell it because he rescently had some shoulder operations and and found it hard to get into and out of the car and he wanted to buy another car. He started it up and I said SOLD! The only real problem is the paint is faded but as far as performance it runs great...and I would have paid twice the amount I got it for (heck maybe more) . I'm going to take some snapshots of it this week end and post them next week to show it off .<P>It could have been in poor condition and I still would have bought it...for the simple reason I have always loved the way they looked and also had the pleasure of driving  one, a 1986 Fiero Se (2m6) and loved how it handled and performed. It feels like a miniture Vette. Simply amazing little sports cars.<P>Well at day break I will examine the wheel and determine if it is infact a bearing or not (thanks for the info on the brake dust shield...i'll check that out).<P>As for the key: It can not be seen so either a locksmith or new locks will be needed I guess (no big deal).<P>As for the cold engine problem. The temp here in Pa. is only about low 40 high 60 so it is not extremely cold yet. The engine when started will fire right up and idle at about 2000rpms for about a second then shut-off. It fires right back up and if you hold the throttle for like 10secs. the car will then hold it own idle right at about 1500rpms<BR>when warm it idles at about 900rpms. I was thinking maybe plugs or wires (or both)...the distribitor and rotor were replace by the previous owner about 2 weeks ago (so that shouldn't be it). I will use the cleaners mentioned on the throttle body and injectors and replace plugs along with a new air filter and see if that cures the problem. If not I will take it to get tuned up by a professional and see if they can correct the problem.<P>Again I would like to thank you guys for the help...keep you posted!||||reg||7
Z||000004||AL||09-29-2001||02:51 AM||||on start up, it sounds like the iac valve is not doing it's job or the cold start injector.<BR><B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||West Coast Fiero||09-29-2001||02:57 AM||||well, try pulling out the IAC valve, do some serious cleaning to the bore in the throttle body where it is located with some brake parts cleaner, clean the heck out of the IAC valve plunger, set the IAC valve to a distance of 1 1/8" from the tip of the plunger to the base of the IAC valve ( do this by rocking the plunger shaft side to side will either pulling or pushing gently ) then re-install<P> Along with this I'd do a full tune up ( plugs, wires, cap, rotor, air filter, fuel filter, change oil and filter, PCV valve, set timing, change trans oil (manual) or fluid and filter ( auto ), degrease engine bay, remove black sound deadener from side of engine bay, im sure there are some things I've forgotten, but start with this<P><P>------------------<BR>Technician, West Coast Fiero<BR>www.cwestco.com<BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||09-29-2001||07:13 AM||||The stalling may be some other "problem"  My 88 automatic has done this since day 1.  I had a remanufactured 3.1L installed, this engine did the same thing.  I had a new 3.4 crate engine with all new components replacing the 3.1  Everything new, except the ECM.  I just live with this fluke.  Once warmed up the car runs fine.||||reg||1
Z||000007||FullRaceCam||09-29-2001||08:20 PM||||remove black sound deadener from side of engine bay,<P>A little bit off topic but this sentence caught my eye. What's the reason - aside from removing a source of itching?||||reg||1
